/-!
# Whole `H¹--H⁻¹` payment of positive restart output work

The actual quadratic convolution is first completed at every Fourier output.
Only then is its time-integrated real work split into positive and negative
parts.  This module pays every finite family of positive output rows directly
from the two whole space-time states generated by the same unforced receipt:

* the inverse-Laplacian weighted viscous row;
* the inverse-Laplacian weighted nonlinear row, recovered as the receipt's
  whole tangent plus that viscous row.

The estimate is cutoff-free.  A finite output set occurs only as the bound
variable of the summability proof; it is not supplied to the producer and the
resulting `tsum` theorem quantifies over the complete integer lattice.
-/

